{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow is a pull_request kernel-build matrix that explicitly sets fail-fast: false and builds against many kernel versions from kernel.org, downloading kernel .deb packages in each build job. I evaluated the applicable patterns. P-LIT-FAIL-FAST (set fail-fast: true) is contraindicated here: every matrix outcome (each kernel-version build) is part of the intended coverage, and the workflow deliberately disables fail-fast; cancelling remaining cells on failure would reduce build/test coverage and hide per-version results, and the supporting evidence is synthetic with a caveat that branch-protection/required-check safety needs separate review. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT (add timeout-minutes) is not safely supported: there is no representative successful-duration history (ci_history shows only failures with no timings), and valid kernel builds can be slow, so an imposed limit risks breaking valid runs (contraindication: valid slow runs exceed the proposed limit). P-LIT-GHA-CACHE (cache dependency downloads) has only observational/illustrative evidence with modest benefit, and its preconditions (repeated measurable dependency fetching with lockfile/environment cache inputs) are not clearly met for versioned kernel .deb downloads, so applying it would be speculative. No other pattern fits (no schedule, no Bazel, no evidenced stale-run problem). No supported change preserves coverage and meets prerequisites.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-GHA-CACHE"]
}
